                <pb facs="0533" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg525"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 (D) Regulations/2313: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-16T19:00:00-05:00">May 16, 1941—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:04 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>180. Reference Department’s telegram no. 98, May 15, noon.<anchor n="49"
                        xml:id="d431-f1"/> The Minister of Finance<anchor n="50" xml:id="d431-f2"/>
                    stated today that the matter must be submitted to the Cabinet for consideration
                    and an official reply is not expected before the end of next week. Informally he
                    said that Peru hesitated to impose a prohibition of exports of domestic
                    products, particularly where contracts had been made for future deliveries.
                    Furthermore, he said that he did not wish to make Peru the spearhead in the
                    imposition of such drastic restrictions for fear of international complications
                    and that he would prefer to see at least four or five of the other American
                    Republics announce such a decision about the same time.</p>
                <p>With respect to the prohibition of the reexportation of products on United States
                    export license list the Minister said that there should be no difficulty in this
                    respect inasmuch as no international question is involved.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
